message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: R
    given-names: Rohan
    affiliation: "The Sainsbury Laboratory, Norwich"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-9225-1775"
title: "Automator: Automated Imaging of Round Petri Dishes/Plates (90-100 mm)"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-26
url: "https://github.com/rotsl/Automator"
abstract: >
  Automator is an open-source system for real-time automated imaging,
  tracking, and analysis of round Petri dishes/plates (90-100 mm). It integrates
  motion control, camera acquisition, and scheduling on Raspberry Pi hardware
  using Klipper, Moonraker, and a custom Python-based controller and web interface.
  Hardware design files are released under CERN-OHL-S-2.0; documentation under CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - automated imaging
  - Petri dishes
  - phenotyping
  - Raspberry Pi
  - Klipper
  - laboratory automation
  - open source hardware
